From 6667a917659b8c6fbdd8e9d705dffda676f4345d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 07:14:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: a setting for how long the boot menu waits

The boot menus of the system wait 10 seconds before they start it by
themselves, which adds to every start where nothing else is chosen.
System > Boot menu offers 10 seconds (the default), 3 or 1, for the GRUB
menu (UEFI) and the syslinux menu (BIOS) alike.

As with the setting of the internal disks, the value is in the menus and
nowhere else: the script of that setting reads it (internal-disks wait)
and changes it (internal-disks wait N) in the menus that this system
makes, with the same checks, lock and written-through copy. Menus that
wait differently, or that this system does not make, hide the setting.
